	abstract     = {The rate at which energetic electrons in amorphous semiconductors lose energy to polar optical phonons, non-polar optical phonons, and acoustic phonons, is calculated. The matrix elements of the electron-phonon interaction are evaluated in the random phase model described in a previous paper. The Shockley hot-electron picture is used, and the field at which the electron temperature becomes appreciably higher than the lattice temperature is estimated to be about 106V/cm in amorphous As2Se3. But in other chalcogenides it may be about 105V/cm, and it is suggested that avalanche ionization may be involved in the switching process in some of these materials.}
}
